      "severity": "important",
      "file": "lib/governance/platform/operations/operationalClosureSource.ts",
      "startLine": 38,
      "endLine": 45,
      "title": "Check original expiry eligibility before fresh native capture",
      "trigger": "Snapshot contains pending/unknown source or derived acquisition, or an issued lease is absent/mismatched in its original private provider-expiry registry, while native assertReadAllowed succeeds.",
      "actual": "assertReadAllowed issues a permit without checking registry eligibility; readEvidence calls captureEvidence before inspecting lease status and original registry records. The request is later refused, but fresh native evidence acquisition has already occurred.",
      "requirement": "Approved section5 requires original expiry plus complete native custody/fleet eligibility resolved before source.readEvidence/fresh acquisition; unknown and unsupported scopes must refuse before acquisition.",
      "fix": "Extract exact original issued-lease/provider/expiry/profile/manifest eligibility preflight. Run it in assertReadAllowed before granting a permit and recheck immediately before captureEvidence after consuming that permit. Retain subsequent native scope receipt checks, immutable metadata comparison and after-await currentness.",
      "validation": "Add source-level intercepted cases for pending/unknown and missing/mismatched source/derived registry metadata; assert captureEvidence is never called and original store emits no event. Existing positive eligible source/owner/drain behavior must remain."
    }
  ],
